From: steam-on-m1-wine
Subject: Optional: continue when the Vulkan device lacks required features

DXVK v3.1.1 skips any Vulkan device that misses a "required" feature
(KosmicKrisp on Metal lacks e.g. fillModeNonSolid), so dxgi.dll finds no
adapter. With the env var DXVK_IGNORE_MISSING_FEATURES set, log a warning
and go on. Only meant for using DXVK's dxgi as the swapchain provider of
vkd3d-proton; D3D11 rendering through this DXVK is not expected to work.

diff --git a/src/dxvk/dxvk_device_info.cpp b/src/dxvk/dxvk_device_info.cpp
index 63d89d9..ecff38d 100644
--- a/src/dxvk/dxvk_device_info.cpp
+++ b/src/dxvk/dxvk_device_info.cpp
@@ -1,3 +1,4 @@
+#include <cstdlib>
 #include <algorithm>
 #include <iomanip>
 #include <set>
@@ -760,6 +761,13 @@ namespace dxvk {
         if (f.extensionEnabled)
           message += str::format(" (extension: ", f.extensionEnabled->extensionName, ")");
 
+        // Metal drivers lack some required features. Only warn, so that
+        // vkd3d-proton can use DXVK's dxgi for its swapchains.
+        if (std::getenv("DXVK_IGNORE_MISSING_FEATURES")) {
+          Logger::warn(message);
+          continue;
+        }
+
         return message;
       }
     }
